# Text payloads embedded with bin2c are installed on the device byte for
# byte, so they must keep LF endings on every checkout. GitHub's Windows
# runners check out with core.autocrlf, which otherwise turns
# patch/pagepedal-usb.sh into "#!/bin/sh\r" and the device can't run it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.qml text eol=lf

# Everything under mods/ is either installed verbatim on the device (scripts,
# systemd units) or patched in byte-for-byte (Tuner_mx5.qml must be exactly
# as long as the source it replaces). Never convert line endings here: a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf would otherwise embed CRLF payloads into
# the installer. (Later lines win, so this overrides the two above for mods/.)
mods/** -text
